## Required treatment-plan contents

For NC Medicaid outpatient specialized therapies, the treatment plan must be created **after the evaluation and before treatment begins**. It must be developed with the medical provider and beneficiary; for children, the parent or legal guardian must be involved, and for adults an authorized representative is included if applicable. It must consider functioning in both clinical and natural environments, be culturally appropriate, and use short- and long-term functional goals and objectives derived from the evaluation. Goals must be reviewed periodically and target measurable functional outcomes. The plan must be a distinct, specific document. [Policy 10A § 3.2.1.6](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment)

**Together with the evaluation or re-evaluation written report, the plan must contain all of the following:**

- Therapy-plan **start and end dates**, with a duration of **no more than six months**;
- The discipline-specific treatment diagnosis and related medical diagnoses;
- The person’s rehabilitative or habilitative potential;
- Defined goals for each therapy discipline that are specific, measurable, and reasonably expected to be achieved during the plan period;
- The skilled interventions, methods, procedures, and particular programs to be used;
- Service frequency;
- Length of each therapy visit, in minutes; and
- The name, credentials, and signature of the professional who completed the plan, dated on or before the plan’s start date. [Policy 10A § 3.2.1.6](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment)

The current Policy 10A version is effective February 1, 2025. [Clinical Coverage Policy 10A](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment)

